@raethlein unfortunately I think you get a CachingReplayClosureError if you try to do what you've suggested. DGs are not hashable, and if you pass them in via a non-hashed argument, there is no way to guarantee that that argument is not `None` or some invalid DG during the replay step, so the code as-written right now raises an error.

My recommendation to the user would be to move the caching decorator to a lower level -- make cached functions for each of the smaller steps, and keep the status block entirely outside of the cache decorator.

```python
import time
import streamlit as st

@st.cache_data
def do_small_step(args):
     st.write(f"small step {args}")
     time.sleep(1)

@st.cache_data
def do_big_step(args)
     for small_step in range(4):
         do_small_step(small_step)
     time.sleep(2)

def show_data():
    with st.status("Downloading data...", expanded=True) as status:
        for big_step in range(3):
            status.update(f"big step {big_step}")
            do_big_step(big_step)

        status.update(
            label="Download complete!", state="complete", expanded=False
        )

show_data()
